  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> moles) reacts completely with acidified aqueous potassium permanganate solution. In this reaction, the number of moles of water produced is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi></math>, and the number of moles of electrons involved is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">y</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "18",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mover><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#10230;</mo><mover><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></mover></math></p><p>The number of electrons involved per molecule is called n-factor.</p><p>n-factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>n-factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Moles</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>factor</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>equivalents</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mo>)</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>MnSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Number of moles of water produced <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>Number of moles of electrons involved <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
